    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d139">

                <pb facs="0339" n="333" sameAs="frus:frus1894app2/pg333"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wharton to Mr.
                            Stevens.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-08-16"><hi rendition="#italic">August 16,
                        1890</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose for your confidential information
                    copy of a letter recently received from the Acting Secretary of the Navy,
                    transmitting one from the commander in chief of the United States naval force in
                    the Pacific station, in regard to political affairs in the Hawaiian Islands. The
                    letter in question seems to confirm the general tenor of your dispatches on the
                    same subject.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William F. Wharton</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
